The matcher in includes/functions.inc.php is adapted from stringmatchlen() in
Redis 7.2 src/util.c:
https://github.com/redis/redis/blob/7.2/src/util.c

Character-class ranges follow the host C char signedness. Redis 7.0.12 on
amd64 compares signed 8-bit values. Redis 7.0.12 on arm64 compares unsigned
8-bit values. PHP ord() is always unsigned.

The adapter evaluates each range twice (signed and unsigned). A key matches
only when both results match. That fail-closed rule never allows a key that
either Redis ABI would exclude. A key that only one ABI would include is
denied (narrow false-deny on high-byte ranges). Equality tests still compare
raw bytes. Escaped class members never start a range.
